    {
      "id": "sl0akbv",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2.4 Climate of Maharashtra"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Maharashtra experiences a tropical monsoon climate. The climate varies significantly between the coastal Konkan region and the inland Deccan plateau.",
      "id": "1o0jr4m"
    },
    {
      "id": "c15e9i4",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Region</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Rainfall</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Climate Characteristics</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Konkan (West of Sahyadri)</p>",
            "<p>2000–4000 mm</p>",
            "<p>Hot and humid; heavy monsoon June–September</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Western Ghats slopes</p>",
            "<p>3000–6000 mm</p>",
            "<p>Heaviest rainfall; Mahabaleshwar receives ~6250 mm</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Deccan Plateau</p>",
            "<p>500–1000 mm</p>",
            "<p>Semi-arid; hot summers, mild winters</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Vidarbha</p>",
            "<p>900–1200 mm</p>",
            "<p>Continental climate; extreme temperatures</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Marathwada</p>",
            "<p>600–900 mm</p>",
            "<p>Drought-prone; irregular monsoon</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "pleyfv3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Highest Rainfall Stations"
    },
    {
      "id": "m4tpn37",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
